# Class-A ULTRA engine (scripts/lib/{explode,detonate}.mjs + tests) is deliberately NOT listed here.
# It was parked under this block as an ungraduated prototype; since the graduation landing (A1-A5) it
# is TRACKED SOURCE, gated by the suite like any other lib. It is kept out of the shipped plugin/ dist
# by the named UNWIRED_ENGINE exclusion in scripts/build-plugin.mjs (enforced in both directions by
# verify.mjs), NOT by this file — and it ships once the class-A SKILL surface wires it. Re-adding it
# here would change nothing in git (the files are tracked) while hiding them from ripgrep and
# re-implying "never ship".

# IC lab scratch — throwaway prototypes/notes, never committed (this is the guard that still serves)
work/

# Internal design specs — process artifacts, not product (CLEAN-CLONE PRINCIPLE: a skill clone
# carries ONLY the skill). Added by MAIN 2026-07-27 after a resident measured that `git add -A`
# would stage two design specs into this PUBLIC repo; main's own dispatch had asserted this dir
# was already fenced, and `git check-ignore` on the DIRECTORY agreed while the FILES were exposed.
# Check the file, never the directory.
docs/

# Board reports — audit output lands INSIDE the scanned part by rule, but it is process, not
# product. Same add -A leak class as docs/ above; caught by station 3 the same day the docs/
# fence went in (an unfenced .coalboard/ would stage the board verdict into this PUBLIC repo).
.coalboard/

